# Dependencies for the transport-candidate benchmark harness ONLY (workdoc step 32).
#
# This file is deliberately separate from pyproject.toml / requirements.lock: pyzmq and
# grpcio are candidates under evaluation, not adopted runtime dependencies. They must
# never leak into the product's requirements.lock. Install into an isolated environment,
# e.g.:
#   uv venv --python 3.13 .venv-transport-bench
#   uv pip sync --python .venv-transport-bench/bin/python requirements.transport-bench.lock
#
# numpy/pydantic/beartype are included so scripts/benchmark_transports.py can reuse
# headcoupled_display.performance.compute_stage_percentiles and headcoupled_display's
# StrictModel/pydantic conventions for its own report schema when run standalone in this
# isolated environment (it is also imported, without these three exercised at runtime,
# from the product .venv's test suite -- see scripts/benchmark_transports.py's docstring).
